      "sequence_position": 8,
      "problem": "If $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{1}{4}$ and $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]=\\frac{9}{4},$ then what is $\\text{Var}[X]?$",
      "worked_solution": "We can compute the variance of a discrete random variable $X$ using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given values, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\frac{9}{4}-{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}-\\frac{1}{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{35}{16}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
